nd a favorite piece of clothing, a boxy denim jacket. It usually goes with a red pencil tucked into a stitched pocket. When somebody else has the floor, Cara counts on the side of one finger where hardly anybody notices.","personality":"Cara has a strong competitive streak and a very soft spot for the person finishing last. A prize tastes better when everybody had enough time to enter.","agenda":"To choose when to read aloud.","family":"Grey Foster is Cara’s first cousin once removed. Cara can always ask for five minutes alone. Grey asks before bringing somebody along. It keeps a conversation between two people from unexpectedly turning into a family committee. Asked about *One sleeve short*, Grey says, “I shortened the sleeve too far on purpose for a child to grow into it.”","connections":"Edgar Carbone (grandparent). A grandparent practicing listening can stay in the room when the child changes languages. Also in the story is Victor Lowe (parent).","familyIds":["AH-R0255"],"connectionIds":["AH-R0962","AH-R0963"],"reactions":[{"situation":"A pupil chooses another language halfway through the reading","response":"Cara lets the pupil finish in the language they chose.","asWritten":"A pupil chooses another language halfway through the reading. Cara lets the pupil finish in the language they chose."},{"situation":"Somebody finds a lost wallet outside the bank","response":"Cara asks the counter staff for a receipt so its return can be traced even after their shift changes.","asWritten":"Somebody finds a lost wallet outside the bank. Cara asks the counter staff for a receipt so its return can be traced even after their shift changes."},{"situation":"If accused of favoritism","response":"Cara explains exactly what help was offered and offers the same practical help to the accuser.","asWritten":"If accused of favoritism, Cara explains exactly what help was offered and offers the same practical help to the accuser."}]},"appearanceSource":"biography casting design"}},{"mesh"